lone-escape-wait

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Wait a set time for the rest of a key or mouse code after a lone trailing ESC before reporting the Esc key, so a read that splits right after the ESC of a mouse report gives no Esc, for a-tui.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream crossterm waits for the rest of a sequence after a lone ESC (crossterm-rs/crossterm#993, #854).
